    "title": "Amber Alert: Enterprise 2-year-old abducted by uncle, police say - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By No media credit provided. ,\n1 hours ago\nDOTHAN, Ala (WDHN) — A search is underway for a 2-year-old believed to have been abducted in Enterprise.\nAn Amber Alert has been issued for 2-year-old Kingston Thomas. He was last seen in the 3400 block of Three Notch Road in Enterprise wearing a yellow shirt and blue shorts.\nEnterprise Police say Thomas is believed to have been abducted by his maternal uncle from a babysitter’s house.\nThe amber alert described the alleged abductor’s car as a blue 2010 Hyundai Genesis with Alabama license plate A21TE2.\nThe suspect’s identity has not been released.\nAnyone with information is asked to call 911 or the Enterprise Police Department at (334) 347-2222.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": ", DOTHAN, Ala (WDHN) — A search is underway for a 2-year-old believed to have been abducted in Enterprise. He was last seen in the 3400 block of Three Notch Road in Enterprise wearing a yellow shirt and blue shorts. Enterprise Police say Thomas is believed to have been abducted by his maternal uncle from a babysitter’s house. The amber alert described the alleged abductor’s car as a blue 2010 Hyundai Genesis with Alabama license plate A21TE2. Anyone with information is asked to call 911 or the Enterprise Police Department at (334) 347-2222.",
